+### Specialty directory
+
+<a id="req-vet-003"></a>
+
+The clinic also publishes the inverse view of that directory. It lists every specialty the clinic knows under the specialty's stored name, and under each one the veterinarians holding it, so staff can ask "who covers dentistry" as readily as "what does this veterinarian cover" `[REQ-VET-003]`. A holder is shown by full name, first name before last. A veterinarian holding no specialty appears nowhere on the page: this is a list of specialties, not the roster. The whole list renders on one page, unpaged, unlike the veterinarian directory.
+
+The page is reachable by its address alone. Nothing in the navigation and no link on any other page leads to it, though the page itself carries the same navigation every page carries `[REQ-SYS-001]`. That absence is deliberate for this round; a visible entry point is a separate request. The page only reads — NG-2 stands, and nothing here creates, changes, or removes a veterinarian or a specialty.
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the clinic's specialties, when the specialty directory is opened, then every one of them is listed under its stored name, all on a single page.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty held by one or more veterinarians, when the directory is opened, then each holder is shown by first name followed by last name.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian appears nowhere on the page.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the navigation and every other page, when they are rendered, then none of them carries a link to the specialty directory.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A specialty that no veterinarian holds is still listed, shown as held by none.
+2. When the clinic knows no specialties at all, the page opens and shows an empty directory rather than failing.
+3. Specialties are presented in a stable order, and so are the veterinarians within each specialty.
+4. Two stored specialties sharing one name are listed as two entries; the page presents stored specialties, not distinct names.
+
+**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts) · **ADR:** [ADR: In-Memory Ordering for Unpaged Listings](adr/2026-08-28-in-memory-ordering-for-unpaged-listings.md)
+
 ### Language
 
